@startuml channel_feishu_option_decision
title Feishu Channel Implementation Options

' Source evidence: larksuite/cli@755daa4de3ea12785c43a15244ffb8f012122c13 skills/lark-event/SKILL.md lines 15-110
' Source evidence: larksuite/cli@755daa4de3ea12785c43a15244ffb8f012122c13 events/im/message_receive.go lines 15-108
' Source evidence: larksuite/channel-sdk-python@731d459cca55ac76e85911bba2b1666508145e03 lark_channel/channel/channel.py lines 289-400 and 780-950
' Source evidence: larksuite/lark-openapi-mcp@21920354ec6e3966b52e89152620c5085e496b55 README.md
' Observed behavior: lark-cli consumes one EventKey per subprocess and emits NDJSON through stdout.
' Observed behavior: lark-mcp exposes OpenAPI tools and is not a durable inbound Channel transport.
' Target-only design: mate-service uses the official Java Server SDK in process; CLI and Python SDK remain alternative adapters.
' Design reason: the Java service must own durable admission, ordering, recovery, and the transactional outbox.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

cloud "Feishu Open Platform" as Feishu

package "Production target" {
  component "Official Java Server SDK\nWS default or Webhook" as JavaSdk
  component "Feishu Provider Adapter" as JavaAdapter
  component "mate-service Channel Core" as ChannelCore
}

package "Alternative adapters" {
  component "Official lark-cli\nevent consume plus im commands" as Cli
  component "CLI Process Adapter\nNDJSON and stderr lifecycle" as CliAdapter
  component "Official Python Channel SDK" as PySdk
  component "Separate Connector Service" as PyConnector
}

package "Separate tool plane" {
  component "Official lark-mcp" as Mcp
  component "Agent Feishu Tools" as Tools
}

Feishu --> JavaSdk : events and OpenAPI
JavaSdk --> JavaAdapter : SDK event types
JavaAdapter --> ChannelCore : normalized message

Feishu --> Cli : local event bus and OpenAPI
Cli --> CliAdapter : stdout NDJSON
CliAdapter ..> ChannelCore : prototype adapter

Feishu --> PySdk : WS or webhook
PySdk --> PyConnector : normalized Channel API
PyConnector ..> ChannelCore : private intake if deployed

Feishu --> Mcp : OpenAPI calls
Mcp --> Tools : MCP tool results
Tools ..> ChannelCore : no inbound ownership

note right of ChannelCore
  Own database deduplication, per-conversation
  ordering, recovery, and outbound outbox.
end note

note bottom of CliAdapter
  Good for local agents and prototypes.
  Not the default multi-instance data plane.
end note

note bottom of Tools
  Tool access does not replace event ingestion.
end note

@enduml

@startuml channel_feishu_target_architecture
title Feishu Channel Target Architecture

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventService.java lines 66-102
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventStream.java lines 48-79 and 107-138
' Source evidence: openclaw/openclaw@b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8 extensions/feishu/src/feishu-ingress.ts lines 330-500
' Source evidence: openclaw/openclaw@b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8 extensions/feishu/src/streaming-card.ts lines 266-403 and 405-726
' Observed behavior: the Runtime POST accepts and persists user.message before starting execution, and disconnect only detaches one stream subscriber.
' Target-only design: no Feishu or Channel implementation exists in mate-service at its analyzed baseline.
' Architecture change: Channel calls the mate-service Chat application port, not CampusClaw directly.
' Design reason: mate-service owns chat_id to session_id mapping and must keep provider identifiers out of CampusClaw.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
top to bottom direction

cloud "Feishu Event Service" as FeishuEvents
cloud "Feishu Message and CardKit APIs" as FeishuApi

package "mate-service" {
  component "Feishu Ingress\nTransport and Provider Adapter" as Ingress
  component "Channel Core\nInbound Service and policy" as ChannelCore
  database "Channel Store\nInbox, binding, execution, delivery, outbox" as Store
  component "Channel Workers\nExecution, reconciliation, projection" as Workers
  component "Chat Boundary\nChannelChatPort and Chat Core" as Chat
  component "Runtime HTTP Client" as RuntimeClient
  component "Feishu Gateway\nMessage and CardKit" as Gateway
  component "Secret Manager Client" as Secrets
}

package "CampusClaw" {
  component "Runtime HTTP API" as RuntimeApi
  component "Session and Active Execution" as RuntimeCore
  database "Session and Entry Store" as RuntimeStore
}

FeishuEvents -down-> Ingress : im.message.receive_v1
Ingress -right-> ChannelCore : verified DTO
ChannelCore -right-> Store : inbox transaction
Store -down-> Workers : claim with lease
Workers -right-> Chat : submit or reconcile
Chat -right-> RuntimeClient : Runtime request
RuntimeClient -down-> RuntimeApi : HTTP and request-scoped SSE
RuntimeApi -right-> RuntimeCore
RuntimeCore -right-> RuntimeStore : durable entries
RuntimeApi .up.> RuntimeClient : SSE or JSON
RuntimeClient .left.> Workers : safe event DTO
Workers .up.> Store : checkpoint and outbox
Store -down-> Gateway : claim delivery task
Gateway -down-> FeishuApi : message and CardKit calls
Ingress .down.> Secrets : app credentials
Gateway .right.> Secrets : token credentials
Chat .up.> Store : chat_id and session_id

note bottom of Ingress
  Provider tenant, user, chat, thread,
  event, and message identifiers end here.
end note

note bottom of Chat
  Local application port in the selected deployment.
  A remote connector needs a separately reviewed
  private intake HTTP contract.
end note

note bottom of RuntimeClient
  Never replay an uncertain POST before
  durable Entry reconciliation succeeds.
end note

@enduml

@startuml channel_feishu_message_sequence
title Feishu Message, Runtime SSE, and Recovery Sequence

' Source evidence: 01-%E6%80%BB%E4%BD%93%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84/01-CampusClaw%E5%A4%9AAgent%E8%BF%90%E8%A1%8C%E6%97%B6/%E6%8E%A5%E5%8F%A3%E5%A5%91%E7%BA%A6/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C/04-submit-user-message.json, submitUserMessage
' Source evidence: 01-%E6%80%BB%E4%BD%93%E6%9E%B6%E6%9E%84/01-CampusClaw%E5%A4%9AAgent%E8%BF%90%E8%A1%8C%E6%97%B6/%E6%8E%A5%E5%8F%A3%E5%A5%91%E7%BA%A6/%E6%93%8D%E4%BD%9C/05-list-session-events.json, listSessionEvents
' Source evidence: larksuite/cli@755daa4de3ea12785c43a15244ffb8f012122c13 events/im/message_receive.go lines 15-108
' Source evidence: larksuite/channel-sdk-python@731d459cca55ac76e85911bba2b1666508145e03 lark_channel/channel/outbound/streaming/markdown_stream.py lines 34-213
' Observed behavior: POST events has no Idempotency-Key and cannot be replayed on an uncertain response.
' Target-only design: persist a pre-submit Entry watermark and reconcile GET events before any retry.
' Product constraint: each Channel conversation exclusively owns its Chat and Runtime Session write path.
' Design reason: the existing Session and Entry contract remains authoritative without restoring a public Run resource.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

autonumber
actor "Feishu user" as User
participant "Feishu Platform" as Feishu
participant "Feishu Adapter" as Adapter
participant "ChannelInboundService" as Inbound
database "Channel Store" as Store
queue "Outbox" as Outbox
participant "ChannelExecutionWorker" as Worker
participant "Chat Application Core" as Chat
participant "CampusClaw Runtime" as Runtime
participant "ChannelEventProjector" as Projector
participant "FeishuMessageGateway" as Gateway

User -> Feishu : send message
Feishu -> Adapter : im.message.receive_v1
Adapter -> Adapter : verify, normalize, and apply policy
Adapter -> Inbound : accept normalized inbound DTO
Inbound -> Store : insert by account_id and message_id

alt duplicate provider message
  Store --> Inbound : existing durable receipt
  Inbound --> Adapter : accepted
  Adapter --> Feishu : handler return
else first provider delivery
  Inbound -> Store : bind conversation and inbox
  Inbound -> Outbox : enqueue PROCESS_INBOUND atomically
  Inbound --> Adapter : durable receipt
  Adapter --> Feishu : handler return

  Outbox -> Worker : claim per-conversation task
  Worker -> Chat : ensure dedicated chat and session mapping
  Chat -> Runtime : create Session when mapping is absent
  Runtime --> Chat : session_id
  Chat -> Store : persist chat_id and session_id before submit
  Worker -> Runtime : GET persisted events from page one
  Runtime --> Worker : current highest entry_seq
  Worker -> Store : persist SUBMITTING and pre_submit_entry_seq
  Worker -> Runtime : POST /sessions/{id}/events as SSE

  alt POST accepted and stream is connected
    Runtime --> Worker : user.message with entry_id and entry_seq
    Worker -> Store : persist accepted Entry identity
    Worker -> Projector : assistant and tool SSE events
    Projector -> Store : checkpoint durable Entry and desired card
    Projector -> Outbox : enqueue coalesced card update
    Outbox -> Gateway : create or update streaming card
    Gateway -> Feishu : CardKit request with sequence and uuid
    Runtime --> Worker : session.status.idle and stream.end
    Worker -> Store : mark execution terminal
  else connection result is uncertain
    Worker -> Store : mark RECONCILING, do not replay POST
    loop until Session is idle or recovery timeout
      Worker -> Runtime : GET Session and GET events from page one
      Runtime --> Worker : state and durable Entries
      Worker -> Store : inspect entry_seq above pre-submit watermark
    end
    alt matching user Entry exists
      Worker -> Store : record accepted Entry and continue final projection
    else no matching Entry and Session is idle
      Worker -> Store : return to READY_TO_SUBMIT
      note right of Worker
        A retry is allowed only after strong-read
        reconciliation proves no acceptance.
      end note
    else ownership or history is ambiguous
      Worker -> Store : mark MANUAL_RECONCILIATION
      Worker -> Gateway : send bounded failure notice
      Gateway -> Feishu : visible terminal result
    end
  end
end

@enduml

@startuml channel_feishu_recovery_state
title Channel Inbound Execution Recovery State

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/persistence/UserEventAcceptance.java lines 17-25
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java@1f801dbb82bdda30478e3354e685e3153b179a0c modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeExecutionCoordinator.java lines 68-82 and 150-164
' Observed behavior: Runtime acceptance is durable before execution starts, while execution completion persists Session idle state.
' Target-only design: Channel state makes uncertain HTTP results explicit and recoverable through durable Entry inspection.
' Design reason: automatic blind replay would duplicate user.message because the current POST has no idempotency key.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

[*] --> ACCEPTED : inbox and outbox committed
ACCEPTED --> READY_TO_SUBMIT : conversation lease acquired
READY_TO_SUBMIT --> SUBMITTING : pre-submit watermark persisted
SUBMITTING --> STREAMING : user.message Entry observed
SUBMITTING --> RECONCILING : HTTP result uncertain
STREAMING --> RECONCILING : SSE disconnected before terminal
STREAMING --> COMPLETED : stream.end and final projection
STREAMING --> FAILED : stream.error and final projection
RECONCILING --> STREAMING : accepted Entry found and Session running
RECONCILING --> COMPLETED : accepted Entry and terminal Entries found
RECONCILING --> READY_TO_SUBMIT : no accepted Entry and Session idle
RECONCILING --> MANUAL_RECONCILIATION : ownership or history ambiguous
MANUAL_RECONCILIATION --> COMPLETED : operator records recovered outcome
MANUAL_RECONCILIATION --> FAILED : operator closes unresolved outcome

note right of RECONCILING
  Do not POST again while acceptance
  remains uncertain.
end note

@enduml
